.TH BITLAFORGE 1 "October 2026" "bitlaForge v1.0.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
bitlaforge \- solo Bitcoin mining, honestly framed
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bitlaforge
.br
.B bitlaforge \-\-version
.br
.B bitlaforge \-\-help
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bitlaForge
is a keyboard-driven terminal application for solo Bitcoin mining as the
lottery it is. It runs
.BR minerd (1)
from the cpuminer project, shows what it is doing in plain words, keeps every
mining session, and shows the real chance of finding a block.
.PP
bitlaForge never starts mining on its own: only
.B M
or the Start button does, and only with a valid wallet. Closing bitlaForge
stops the miner, after asking. The miner is started under
.B setpriv \-\-pdeathsig TERM
so that the system stops it if bitlaForge ends without a chance to.
.PP
Only Bitcoin is mined (the sha256d method). The wallet address is checked on
the computer (Base58Check, bech32, bech32m); nothing is sent to check it.
.PP
No root privileges are needed. The full manual is inside the application
(Help \(-> Manual, or
.B F1
on a setting) and in
.I /usr/lib/bitlaforge/bitlaforge/manual/
as Markdown.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print the usage and exit.
.
.SH SCREENS
.TP
.B 1 \- Dashboard
Mining state and pool; speed now and on average, a chart of the last 30
minutes and a bar per core; the chance of a block today and this year;
processor temperature, the miner's processor use, priority and shares.
.TP
.B 2 \- Settings
Pool & wallet (solo pools from a list, or Other; the wallet checked as it is
typed; worker name), Miner (cores to use; Gentle or Normal priority), Safety
(pause when hot and at what temperature; lottery odds).
.TP
.B 3 \- Log
The miner's output, the important lines in plain words. Show: Important,
Everything, Problems, Shares. The wallet is never shown.
.TP
.B 4 \- History
Every mining session, kept between runs, with why it stopped, and the totals.
.
.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B M
Start or stop mining.
.TP
.B T
Test the miner: 10 seconds on one core, without a pool.
.TP
.B 1 \(en 4 ", " Ctrl+letter
Go to a screen.
.TP
.B Tab ", " Shift+Tab
Next / previous field or button.
.TP
.B Enter
Open a list, press a button, confirm.
.TP
.B Space
Flip a switch.
.TP
.B Up ", " Down
In a number: step through its presets.
.TP
.B Esc
Close a window, or leave a field.
.TP
.B F10 ", " S
Save settings, with a review first.
.TP
.B R
Read the settings file again; unsaved changes stay.
.TP
.B F1
Help on what is selected.
.TP
.B / ", " F ", " C
In the Log: find, follow on or off, clear.
.TP
.B ?
All keys.
.TP
.B Q ", " Ctrl+Q
Quit; stops the miner, after asking.
.
.SH SAFETY
A save shows every change (old \(-> new), backs the file up first and writes
it in one step; anything else in the file is kept. A settings file that cannot
be read is never saved over; the newest backup is offered instead.
.PP
With Pause when hot on (the default), the miner is paused (SIGSTOP) when the
processor reaches the limit (85 \(deC by default) and resumed (SIGCONT) 5
\(deC lower. The temperature comes from the processor's own sensor
(k10temp, zenpower, coretemp or cpu_thermal under
.IR /sys/class/hwmon ).
.PP
With Lottery odds on (the default), mempool.space is asked once an hour for
the network's difficulty and the last block's reward. Nothing about the user
is sent.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/bitlaforge/config.toml
The settings. Read and written by bitlaForge.
.TP
.I ~/.config/bitlaforge/backups/
Backups (the newest 20), each with a note saying why it was made.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bitlaforge/history.json
Every mining session.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/bitlaforge/logs/
One line per run, by day.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/bitlaforge/network.json
The last answer from mempool.space.
.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
Linux; Python 3.11 or newer; python-textual, python-rich, python-tomlkit and
python-forgekit 0.5.1 or newer; util-linux. To mine:
.B minerd
(the cpuminer package on Arch and openSUSE; elsewhere the cpuminer project's
ready-made program, see the manual).
.
